Overlay patch 0055 (D35): REAL-TIME TICK CATCH-UP + the LH_PACE probe.
Port of Shipwright-ios 0065 (D-084), by way of Starship-ios 0041.

THE SEAM. GameEngine::ProcessGfxCommands (Lighthouse's Graph_ProcessGfxCommands)
runs once per game tick -- once per RCP task the game thread hands the window
thread -- and renders `subframesPerTick` = interpolation fps / logic Hz frames
for it (BK logic is 30 Hz, D6: 4 frames per tick at 120). Frame i of n is
drawn with matrices interpolated at t = i/n (mtx_replacements[0..n-1], the last
one empty = the tick's real state).

WHAT IS DIFFERENT FROM SOH. BK's logic runs on its own thread, paced by the
60 Hz VI ticker (src/port/OS/OS_VI.cpp, an absolute schedule), and upstream
already guards the pass: RunCommands stops a pass whose remaining tick budget
(sPassBudgetNs) is smaller than the last sub-frame took -- dropping the LATER
frames, including the real-state one. What nothing looks at is the wall clock
ACROSS ticks: a pass that overruns still delays the SP/DP done events the game
thread syncs on. This patch adds SoH's debt rule beside upstream's guard, it
does not replace it: debt = real time between passes minus the tick period
(viPerTick / 60 s, exact for cutscene and demo VI counts), clamped to
[0, one tick], reset by any stall over 250 ms. While the debt is at least one
frame period, the EARLIEST interpolated frames of this tick are not built at
all (their FrameInterpolation_Interpolate never runs) -- never the last one.
gSohIos.TickCatchup (default 1) is the A/B switch; 3D (visionOS immersive) is
left alone. RunCommands keeps its blend factors keyed to the ORIGINAL frame
count (SOHIOS_SKIP), so a skipped tick still blends anim vertices at
t = (k + skip) / n. (Its `frameCount > 1 || IsFrameReady()` gate needs no
edit: the SDL2 window backend's IsFrameReady() is always true.)

THE PROBE (no behaviour change): one `LH_PACE` line per 10 s beside LH_PERF:
tick wall p50/p95/max + tps, and each 2D frame split into
  wait  -- inside SetupScreenFramebuffer (nextDrawable / background park)
  busy  -- drawable acquired -> SwapBuffersBegin: the CPU work of the frame
  sleep -- LUS's SyncFramerateWithTime nanosleep pacer
plus frames skipped, ticks that skipped, debt, thermal and power state
(shell SohIos_PowerState: Low Power Mode caps the panel at 60 Hz).
gSohIos.PaceStressMs (default 0, test instrument) busy-waits that many ms per
frame so the catch-up can be proven on a simulator.

Code lives in new files src/port/SohIosPace.{h,cpp} (source of truth:
overlay/assets/probe/); the vendor hunks are call sites only. Generated by
scripts/lh_genlib.py against each file's state just before this patch, so it
regenerates byte-identically from a pristine or a fully patched tree.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/port/SohIosPace.h
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+// LIGHTHOUSE_IOS (overlay 0055, D35): pace probe + real-time tick catch-up --
+// shared state for the later probes (0056 spike probe, 0057 menu split).
+// Port of Shipwright-ios 0065 (D-084) via Starship-ios 0041. iOS only.
+#pragma once
+#ifdef __IOS__
+#include <chrono>
+
+namespace SohIosPace {
+using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
+// Pace seams of the most recent 2D frame (render thread = the main thread):
+//   gDrawBegin  -> gDrawEnd    nextDrawable (SetupScreenFramebuffer)
+//   gDrawEnd    -> gSleepBegin the frame's CPU work
+//   gSleepBegin -> ...         LUS's SyncFramerateWithTime nanosleep pacer
+extern Clock::time_point gDrawBegin, gDrawEnd, gSleepBegin;
+// Interpolation fps of the current tick (frame period = 1000 / gFps ms).
+extern int gFps;
+inline double Ms(Clock::time_point a, Clock::time_point b) {
+    return std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(b - a).count();
+}
+inline bool Set(Clock::time_point t) {
+    return t.time_since_epoch().count() != 0;
+}
+} // namespace SohIosPace
+
+extern "C" {
+// Called by GameEngine::ProcessGfxCommands once per game tick (one RCP task =
+// one tick's display list), before the interpolated frames are built: returns
+// how many of this tick's EARLIEST frames to drop (0..frames-1) and feeds the
+// LH_PACE report. viPerTick: 60 Hz VIs per tick (2 = BK's 30 Hz, more in
+// cutscenes and demo replays), so the tick period is viPerTick / 60 s exactly.
+int SohIos_TickCatchup(int fps, int viPerTick, int frames);
+void SohIos_PaceDrawableBegin(void);
+void SohIos_PaceDrawableEnd(void);
+void SohIos_PaceSleepBegin(void);
+void SohIos_PaceSleepEnd(void);
+int SohIos_ThermalState(void);
+int SohIos_PowerState(void); // shell: 1 LPM, 2 charging, 4 full, 8 unknown
+extern volatile int gSoh3DMode;
+}
+#endif
